hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17620","Hushaym narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his brother Mutarrif ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds a lost item, let him call just witnesses and preserve its container and its tie. If its owner comes, let him not conceal it, and he has most right to it. If its owner does not come, then it is wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: I said to my father: Some people say 'iqasaha and say 'ifasaha. He said: 'Ifasaha, with fa'."
"17621","Hushaym narrated to us: Ibn 'Awn informed us, from al-Hasan, from 'Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashi'i, and there was acquaintance between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he was sent. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, he gave him a gift, I think it was camels, but he refused to accept it and said: We do not accept the zabad of the polytheists. He said: I said: What is the zabad of the polytheists? He said: Their support, their gift."
"17622","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man from my people reviles me, and he is inferior to me; is there harm upon me if I retaliate against him? He said: Two persons reviling each other are two devils accusing one another and lying against one another."
"17623","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon one day and said in his sermon: My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of from what He taught me on this day of mine. Every wealth I have granted My servants is lawful, and I created My servants as upright all of them. The devils came to them, led them astray from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, looked at the people of the earth and abhorred them, their non-Arabs and their Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. And He said: I have sent you only to test you and to test others through you. I have sent down upon you a Book which water cannot wash; you recite it sleeping and waking. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to burn Quraysh, so I said: O Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like bread. He said: Drive them out as they drove you out, fight them and We will support you, spend on them and We will spend on you, send an army and We will send five like it, fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you. The people of Paradise are three: a just, charitable, guided ruler; a merciful man, tender-hearted toward every relative and Muslim; and a poor, chaste, charitable man. The people of Fire are five: the weak who has no restraint, those among you who are followers, Yahya doubted, whether he said followers or dependents, seeking neither family nor wealth; the traitor whose greed is not hidden from him, however slight, except he betrays it; a man who does not begin morning or evening except deceiving you about your family and wealth; and he mentioned miserliness and lying, and the foul-mouthed obscene person."
"17624","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Mutarrif narrate this hadith, and 'Affan said in the hadith of Hammam: And the foul-mouthed obscene person. He said: And he mentioned lying or miserliness."
"17625","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah, from his brother, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The sin of two persons reviling each other, for what they both said, is upon the initiator until the wronged one transgresses, or unless the wronged one transgresses, Yazid doubted."
"17626","Bahz narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two persons reviling each other are two devils lying against one another and reviling one another."
"17627","Bahz and 'Affan said: Hammam narrated to us. 'Affan said in his hadith: Qatadah narrated to us, from Yazid, brother of Mutarrif, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sin of two persons reviling each other, for what they both said, is upon the initiator so long as he does not transgress. 'Affan said: Or until the wronged one transgresses."
"17628","Yunus narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: And Mutarrif narrated, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what do you think of a man who reviles me while he is inferior to me in lineage? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two persons reviling each other are two devils reviling one another and lying against one another."
"17629","'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from 'Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon one day: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to teach you, and he mentioned the hadith, except he said: Those among you who are followers, seeking no family. And he mentioned lying and miserliness. Sa'id said: Mutarrif said, from Qatadah: The foul-mouthed obscene person."
